      "summary": {
        "headline": "Transaction mail per household: published values for FY2025 and how they moved.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "In FY2025, Transaction mail per household was 93.7 (pieces per household per year). That fell by 17.3 (15.6%) from the previous year, FY2024. That fell by 47.5 (33.6%) from five years earlier, FY2020.",
            "metric": "transactions-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025,
              2024,
              2020
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By income in FY2025, Transaction mail per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for $150,000 and Over at 109.1 and lowest for Less than $50,000 at 81.6.",
            "metric": "transactions-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By age in FY2025, Transaction mail per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for 65 and Over at 133.4 and lowest for Under 45 at 51.8.",
            "metric": "transactions-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By education in FY2025, Transaction mail per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for Some college or technical school graduate at 99.3 and lowest for Less than high school at 87.6.",
            "metric": "transactions-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By msa in FY2025, Transaction mail per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for Non-MSA at 101.8 and lowest for Large MSA at 89.4.",
            "metric": "transactions-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By tenure in FY2025, Transaction mail per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for Own at 114.5 and lowest for Rent at 53.8.",
            "metric": "transactions-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
          "Methodology change in FY2024: New contractor and per-household reporting. Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Methodology change in FY2025: Household Mail Survey redesign. Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Household-group bands (age, income, education) were redefined over time, so group comparisons across years should be read with the methodology notes."
        ]
      },
